# Git LFS — large binary files (game builds, assets, media)
# Docs: https://git-lfs.github.com/
# After cloning, run once locally:  git lfs install
# Then add files normally:          git add <file> && git commit && git push
# GitHub limits without LFS: 25 MB in browser, 100 MB via git push (50 MB warning).
# With LFS: up to 2 GB per file (Free/Pro). Free LFS quota: 1 GB storage + 1 GB bandwidth/mo.
# NOTE: LFS files must be added AFTER this file is committed, otherwise they are stored as normal git blobs.

